Patches applied to the pristine acl-2.4.0 tarball by ../unpack.sh.

They apply with `patch -p1` from inside src/, in filename order.  Each one
starts with a few lines of prose saying what it does and why, then the diff.
0001 and 0002 are the attr port's (ports/attr-2.6.0/patches) for acl's own copy of
the same helper library.

  0001-xattrat-syscall-header-only-with-syscalls.patch
        libmisc/xattrat.c includes the header defining struct xattr_args
        only when the *xattrat system call numbers exist; without them its
        stand-ins answer ENOSYS and never use the structure.

  0002-proc-self-fd-likeos-descriptor-paths.patch
        A name relative to a directory descriptor (getfacl -R, setfacl -R,
        setfacl --restore, acl_get_file_at() ...) is reached through the
        path the descriptor was opened with, read from the /proc/self/fd/N
        link, instead of through /proc/self/fd/N/<name>, which the path walk
        does not cross.

  0003-uid-gid-lookup-undefined-id-unsigned.patch
        "4294967295" is refused as a user or group id (it is
        ACL_UNDEFINED_ID) also with the LikeOS libc's signed id_t.

